 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nhost_from_uri function returns incorrect format\n\nDescription\n\nThe `host_from_uri` function in `oauthlib/oauth2/rfc6749/utils.py` is returning the hostname and port in an incorrect format. Instead of returning a tuple of (hostname, port), it's returning a string with the format \"hostname:port\".\n\nThis breaks code that expects the function to return a tuple, which was the previous behavior.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.utils import host_from_uri\n\n# Before the change:\n# Would return ('example.com', '443')\n# Now returns 'example.com:443'\nresult = host_from_uri('https://example.com/path')\nprint(result)  # Now prints 'example.com:443' instead of a tuple\n\n# This will now fail with a TypeError since you can't unpack a string\nhostname, port = host_from_uri('https://example.com/path')\n```\n\nThe issue affects any code that relies on unpacking the return value of `host_from_uri` into hostname and port variables.\n</issue>\n",
